.scratch/

# Workstation tunnel daemon hardcodes the real seedbox FQDN — treat as secret.
scripts/manitoba-tunnel.ps1

# scripts/local-llm/qflix-rea.ps1 was listed here until 2026-09-27. It is now
# TRACKED, by operator decision, for archival: the repo should carry the history
# of the alerting layer rather than a mirror of its latest bytes.
# It was never excluded for secrets. Re-verified at the moment it was enrolled:
# no FQDN (Resolve-SshHost reads secrets/seedbox.ssh-host at runtime and throws
# rather than guess), no token, no credential, no member data. The only two
# identifiers it carries — the slot nickname "manitoba" and the orphaned Plex
# Discord webhook ID in the noise regex — were already in 332 tracked files and
# in manifest/rea-noise-classes.yaml, so tracking it exposed nothing new.
# Consequences, all landed in the same commit: it leaves audit-scope surface S2
# (so backup-untracked.ps1 no longer enrols it — git does that now), and the
# pwsh CI job runs its 519-case suite unconditionally instead of skipping it.

# Staging dir for the 2026-05-11 inventory-driven cleanup; safe to delete once
# the operator confirms nothing was accidentally swept.
.purged-*/
.admin-key/
